e the old text. The page reads them as plain values, so the HTML it produces has the same shape as before. Tests that used to pass these through `createApp` now build `State({ heading, badgeLabel })` and render the page from source.\n2. **Paths outside the prefix.** These now get a new route, `NOT_FOUND_ROUTE` (`'/404'`, in `pages/routes.ts`), so they render the not-found page with a 404. Before, a request for `/list` outside the prefix rendered the real list page with a 404 status. I also made the prefix check stricter: a path like `/example-hydrationx` now counts as outside the prefix, where before it was read as under it.\n3. **`/index.html`.** Under the prefix it now maps to route `/`, so the nav marks the home link as current. I removed `/index.html` from `ROUTES`, since it is no longer a route of its own.\n4. **Tests.** Each change started with a failing test in `test/hydration.ts` (red, then green). Final runs all passed: `test:hydration` (126 tests, plus 17 in the listener test), `test:hydration-dev` (17), `npm test` (413), lint, both typechecks, and `test:e2e` (12).\n\nI updated `example-hydration/README.md` and re-ran `toc:hydration`, and added a note to `AGENTS.md` on the state-only rule and how routes are worked out. Notes for the next attempt are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is not committed.\n\nI left the existing test for the `reduce-fouce` opacity gate alone, because removing that gate belongs to a different ticket. A fresh worktree needs `npm run build` before `test:hydration` will run.","ttft_ms":2948,"type":"result","duration_ms":301154,"uuid":"6dd3d7cc-2bc3-4bfc-b81a-c3c6fe2842de","ttft_stream_ms":2211,"time_to_request_ms":391,"first_content_frame_ms":2212,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
